WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:08.233
In this walkthrough we'll understand
what closing an accounting period does
before you do it, in the OpenTRMS Workbench.

2
00:00:08.233 --> 00:00:18.900
Closing an accounting period draws a line under it.
Once closed, no further entries can be booked into
that period, which is what makes the reported numbers final.

3
00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:31.300
The Workbench marks this as a destructive action, and says
plainly that it cannot be quickly undone. That warning is
the pattern for anything consequential — if you see it, read it.

4
00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:40.933
The only input is the period itself. There
is deliberately nothing else to configure,
because a close either happens or it does not.

5
00:00:40.933 --> 00:00:53.000
Before closing, the work is done elsewhere. Draft journal
entries need posting, and anything still pending approval
needs resolving, because neither can be added afterwards.

6
00:00:53.000 --> 00:01:02.667
Start Close commits it. In a shared
environment this affects everyone, so it is
worth being certain the period is genuinely complete.

7
00:01:02.667 --> 00:01:11.033
That completes Closing an Accounting Period. Every
surface shown here can also be opened from the agent
panel on the right, by asking for it in plain English.
